From 2710120c848fab519122b16bc9a04e497bece770 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amir <hello@noury.ch>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:48:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/32] feat(ui): accept on Enter/Right, and actually style the
 dropdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Accepting a suggestion required Tab; Enter always submitted and Right always
moved the cursor, which made the dropdown feel unresponsive.

- Enter and Right arrow now accept too, via a single #isAcceptKey/#pendingAcceptance
  pair so tab/enter/right cannot diverge. Both are config-gated (acceptOnEnter,
  acceptOnRightArrow, default true).
- Right arrow only accepts with the cursor at end of line (cursorTerminated);
  mid-line it must keep moving the cursor or the line becomes uneditable.
- Enter must not clear the command when it is going to accept, or it would wipe
  the very line the acceptance edits — so the acceptance is resolved BEFORE the
  existing clearCommand() on return.
- An exact match needs no second Enter: calculateReplacement() already returns
  undefined when only a trailing space would be inserted, so the key falls
  through and submits.

Styling, now a [theme] table (border, activeBackground, activeForeground,
description, pointer):
- borders are coloured — renderBox always accepted a borderColor but no caller
  ever passed one.
- selected row gets a pointer in a fixed-width gutter present on every row, so
  the text does not shift as the selection moves, plus bold + accent background
  spanning the full row.
- description panel text is dimmed so the list stays dominant.

Fixes a latent bug this exposed: renderBox did
`chalk.hex(borderColor).apply(text)`, which calls Function.prototype.apply with
text as thisArg and NO arguments, so chalk returned an empty string and every
border character vanished. Dormant only because borderColor was never passed.
Verified display width is a uniform 40 cells for both emoji and 1-wide icons.
